[Event "Scandinavian: 3...Qa5"]

{The Scandinavian (1...d5) challenges e4 at once. Black accepts some loss of time with the queen for a clear, solid structure.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] The Scandinavian. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
2. exd5 {Takes.}
2... Qxd5 {Recaptures. The queen on d5 eyes the pawn on a2 and the pawn on d2 and controls d4 and e4 and e5.}
3. Nc3 {Gains time on the queen. The knight on c3 eyes the queen on d5 and controls e4.}
3... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c3] The queen pins the knight. The queen on a5 eyes the knight on c3 and the pawn on a2 and controls d5 and e5.}
 (3... Qd6 {The modern retreat. The queen on d6 eyes the pawn on d2 and the pawn on h2 and controls d4 and d5 and e5.}
4. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
4... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
5. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... a6 {Stops Nb5.}
6. g3 {Fianchetto.}
6... Bg4 {Develops. The bishop on g4 eyes the knight on f3.}
)
4. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
4... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
5. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... c6 {Gives the queen d8 and stops Nb5. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
 (5... Bf5 {Develops the bishop before ...c6. The bishop on f5 eyes the pawn on c2 and controls e4.}
6. Bd2 {[%cal Gd2a5] Unpins, with Nd5 or Bc4 ideas against the queen.}
6... c6 {Now covers d5 and b5. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
)
6. Bc4 {Develops. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
6... Bf5 {Develops outside the chain. The bishop on f5 eyes the pawn on c2 and controls e4.}
7. Bd2 {Unpins.}
7... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.} *

[Event "Scandinavian: 3.Nf3 & 3.d4"]

{White can delay Nc3.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... d5 {Scandinavian. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
2. exd5 {Takes.}
2... Qxd5 {Recaptures. The queen on d5 eyes the pawn on a2 and the pawn on d2 and controls d4 and e4 and e5.}
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
 (3. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
4. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
4... Bf5 {Develops. The bishop on f5 eyes the pawn on c2 and controls e4.}
5. c4 {Gains time. The pawn on c4 eyes the queen on d5.}
5... Qd8 {Safe retreat. The queen on d8 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls d5.}
)
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
4. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
4... Bg4 {Pins. The bishop on g4 eyes the knight on f3.}
5. Be2 {Unpins.}
5... e6 {Solid.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
7. c4 {Gains time. The pawn on c4 eyes the queen on d5.}
7... Qh5 {Retreats. The queen on h5 eyes the pawn on h2 and controls d5 and e5.} *
